<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xri version="1.0">
   <description><p>BlackRig scripts for PixInsight, by Erellaz.</p></description>
   <platform os="all" arch="noarch" version="1.9.0:2.0.0">
      <package fileName="DebandDesat-1.0-20261120.zip" sha1="9d62e4457c431f0edeef9e28dc111add8d2d3d29" type="script" releaseDate="20261120">
         <title>DebandDesat</title>
         <description><p>Deband 2.1, Desat 3.0 and their WBPP pipeline builders (Deband_WBPP 1.0, Desat_WBPP 1.4, DebandDesat_WBPP 1.0), with TrailBlink 1.2 and AdaptiveSubtraction 1.2, by Erellaz (MIT license).</p><p>Deband removes CMOS row and column banding and periodic pattern noise in the Fourier domain, with star protection. Desat removes satellite trails from registered light frames by comparing each frame with a trail-free stack of the same frames and subtracting only the trail (new in 3.0: the faint wings of bright trails are removed too). Both run on open frames, in batch, or inside WeightedBatchPreprocessing. AdaptiveSubtraction removes an unwanted signal from an image by subtracting a reference image or model of it (a star model, a trail, a gradient), matched to the image locally by robust least squares; it works on two open images.</p><p>After installing: Script &gt; BlackRig &gt; Deband, Desat, TrailBlink and AdaptiveSubtraction. For WBPP, select src/scripts/BlackRig/DebandDesat/Desat_WBPP.js (trails only), Deband_WBPP.js (banding only) or DebandDesat_WBPP.js (banding before registration, then trails) in the PixInsight installation folder as WBPP's pipeline builder (Pipeline tab).</p><p>Documentation: Desat_quick_start.pdf in the same folder.</p><p>Renamed in November 2026 (SatelliteTrailRemover is now Desat, FourierDeband is now Deband, TrailLabeler is now TrailBlink; saved parameters carry over). After updating, delete the folder src/scripts/BlackRig/SatelliteTrailRemover of an earlier installation, and any separate copy of FourierDeband, so the old names leave the Script menu. Likewise delete any separate copy of AdaptiveSubtraction, or it appears twice in the menu.</p></description>
      </package>
   </platform>
</xri>
